---
title: Slow Cooker Lamb Shanks
servings: 4
prepTime: 10 min
cookTime: 4 hr
difficulty: Easy
Rating: 8/10
description: No need to brown the shanks before adding to the crock pot.
source: https://healthyrecipesblogs.com/slow-cooker-lamb-shanks/
tags: Lamb, Slow Cooker
---

> Note: Pre-seasoned lamb shanks (such as rosemary-rubbed) work excellent for this recipe.
> Just add the prepared shanks to the broth, without adding any additional seasonings.

Add the @beef broth{2%Cups} to your #slow cooker{}.

Season the @lamb shanks{3%lb} with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1/4%tsp},
@garlic powder{1/2%tsp}, @ground cumin{1/2%tsp}, and @dried rosemary{1/2%tsp}.
Place the shanks in your slow cooker. 

Cover and cook on HIGH for ~{4%hours} or LOW for ~{7%hours}, until the lamb is very tender. 
While the lamb is cooking, prepare @?mashed potatoes{}(optional) or other side dishes.

When the lamb shanks finish cooking, set the slow cooker to WARM.
Transfer the cooked lamb shanks to a plate.

Strain the cooking liquids into a glass measuring cup, then return the lamb
to the slow cooker pan and cover, to keep warm while you thicken the gravy.

Use a spoon to skim the fat layer off the top of the cooking juices.
Pour them into a medium #saucepan{}.
Heat over medium-high heat until almost boiling but not quite, then turn the heat down
to medium and simmer, whisking occasionally.
Combine @cornstarch{1%tbsp} with @water{1%tbsp} in a small bowl, and add to the sauce.
Cook until liquids are reduced into a rich gravy, ~{10-15%minutes}. 

Transfer the lamb shanks to plates, spoon the gravy on top, and serve with potatoes or other side dishes.
